sudo cp promtool /usr/local/bin/


It should return:

```
SUCCESS: 4 rules found
```

Then reload Prometheus (depending on setup):

```bash
systemctl restart prometheus
```

OR

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:9090/-/reload
```

#Task 3: Configure Alertmanager Routing and Receivers
🎯 Objective
Create an alertmanager.yml configuration that intelligently routes, groups, and suppresses alerts received from Prometheus.

📝 Instructions
Update the /root/assets/alertmanager/alertmanager.yml file with the following configuration goals:

🌐 Global Section: Set resolve_timeout to 5m to automatically resolve inactive alerts after 5 minutes.
🧩 Root Route:
Default receiver: default-receiver
Group alerts by alertname, severity, and service
Use group_wait: 10s, group_interval: 30s, and repeat_interval: 12h
🚦 Sub-Routes:
Critical alerts → Send to critical-receiver with group_wait: 5s and repeat_interval: 5m
Warning alerts → Send to warning-receiver with group_wait: 30s and repeat_interval: 30m
🚫 Inhibition Rules:
If ServiceDown alert is active, silence HighErrorRate and HighRequestLatency alerts for the same service.
If a critical alert exists, suppress all warning alerts for that service.
📬 Receivers:
default-receiver → http://sample-app:5000/webhook/default
critical-receiver → http://sample-app:5000/webhook/critical
warning-receiver → http://sample-app:5000/webhook/warning
Ensure each receiver has send_resolved: true enabled so resolution notifications are delivered.

💡 Tip: Test routing using Prometheus’s amtool or by manually triggering alerts from the alert_rules.yml file you created earlier.